_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 34
---
order: 34
---
short_label: III.34
---
statement: From a given circle to cut off a segment admitting an angle equal to a given rectilinear angle. </font color>
---
red_highlight: yes
---
proof:

Let *ABC* be the given circle, and the angle at *D* the given rectilinear angle.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="320" height="240" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="III.34 diagram" src="propIII34.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "canvas_0",
        background: "35,19,100",
        title: "III.34",
        elements: [
            "D1;point;free;290,120;0",
            "D2;point;free;240,180;0",
            "D3;point;free;300,180;0",
            "D12;line;connect;D1,D2",
            "D23;line;connect;D2,D3",
            "D;polygon;triangle;D1,D2,D3;black;0;0;0",
            "A;point;free;185,195",
            "E;point;free;30,210",
            "F;point;free;30,30",
            "EF;line;connect;E,F",
            "B;point;lineSlider;EF,30,120",
            "BO';line;perpendicular;B,E;0;0;0",
            "M;point;midpoint;B,A;0;0",
            "MM';line;perpendicular;M,A;0;0;0",
            "O;point;intersection;BO',MM';0;0",
            "ABC;circle;radius;O,B;0;0;black;random",
            "C';point;similar;F,B,D1,D2,D3;0;0",
            "BC;line;chord;B,C',ABC;0;0;0",
            "C;point;last;BC",
            "triABC;polygon;triangle;A,B,C;0;0;black;random"
        ],
    });
</script>
</figure>

It is required to cut off from the circle *ABC* a segment admitting an angle equal to the given rectilinear angle, the angle at *D.*

Draw *EF* touching *ABC* at the point *B.*  Construct the angle *FBC* equal to the angle at *D* on the straight line *FB* and at the point *B* on it. [!just III.17; I.23]

Then, since a straight line *EF* touches the circle *ABC,* and *BC* has been drawn across from the point of contact at *B,* the angle *FBC* equals the angle constructed in the alternate segment *BAC.* [!just III.32]

But the angle *FBC* equals the angle at *D,* therefore the angle in the segment *BAC* equals the angle at *D.*

Therefore from the given circle *ABC* the segment *BAC* has been cut off admitting an angle equal to the given rectilinear angle, the angle at *D.*

<div class="qed">Q.E.F.</div>
<br clear="all">
---
body:

This proposition is not used in the rest of the *Elements.*
